  "id": "COMPOUND:28197 - PROTEIN:367",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Divaricataester C and S-methylmethionine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase BHMT2, as all three paths indicate that Divaricataester C acts as a target of multiple entities, which in turn target BHMT2. Specifically, Divaricataester C is linked to Serine--tRNA ligase, a protein that is targeted by certolizumab pegol and by 13-[(2R,3R,4R)-3,4-dihydroxy-2-(hydroxymethyl)-3,4-dihydro-2H-pyrrol-5-yl]-1-hydroxytridecan-5-one, both of which are known to target BHMT2. Additionally, Divaricataester C is also linked to everolimus, which is known to target BHMT2. This suggests that Divaricataester C may be involved in a broader network of interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition of BHMT2. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, indicating a possible functional relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated.",
